  "content": "<!-- Header Section End -->\n\n            <!-- Content Wrapper Start -->\n            <div class=\"content-wrapper\">\n\n                <!-- Breadcrumb Start -->\n                <div class=\"breadcrumb-wrap bg-f br-1\">\n                    <div class=\"container\">\n                        <div class=\"breadcrumb-title\">\n                            <h2>Member Profile</h2>\n                            <ul class=\"breadcrumb-menu list-style\">\n                                <li><a href=\"/\">Home </a></li>\n                                <li><a href=\"/team\">Our Team</a></li>\n                                <li>Profile</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <!-- Breadcrumb End -->\n\n                <!-- Volunteer Details Section Start -->\n                <section class=\"team-details-wrap ptb-100\">\n                    <div class=\"container\">\n                        <div class=\"row gx-5\">\n                            <div class=\"col-lg-8 order-lg-1 order-2\">\n                                <div class=\"team-desc\">\n                                    <h1>Usman Felix Cole</h1>\n                                    <p>Osman Felix Cole is a dedicated environmental advocate and accomplished Project/Program Manager, renowned for his invaluable contributions to the field of environmental and climate justice. With a career spanning over five years, Osman has established himself as a leader in the promotion of sustainability, climate-smart agriculture, and environmental human rights.</p>\n                                    <h5><strong>Professional Journey</strong></h5>\n\n                                           <p> Osman's journey in the realm of environmental advocacy began with his role as Project/Program Manager for the Earth Regenerative Project Sierra Leone (EaRP-SL), a prominent NGO. In this capacity, he has diligently worked to address critical environmental issues and drive positive change within Sierra Leone.</p>\n                                   \n                                    \n                                    <h5><strong>Environmental and Climate Justice Advocate</strong></h5>\n                                    <p>Throughout his career, Osman has tirelessly championed environmental and climate justice causes. His core focus areas include capacity-building, public participation, climate-smart agriculture, and the protection of environmental human rights. His work demonstrates a profound commitment to fostering a sustainable future for our planet.</p>\n\n                                    <h5><strong>Global Engagement</strong></h5>\n                                    <p>Osman's dedication extends beyond national borders. He played a pivotal role at World Education International (WEI) in Boston, Massachusetts, a respected 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization. Here, he specialized in climate and environmental education, as well as climate-smart agriculture. Osman's impact was felt through educational workshops and events conducted for teachers, school principals, students, education representatives, and citizen activists across multiple educational institutions in the region.</p>\n\n                                    <h5><strong>Leadership and Advocacy</strong></h5>\n                                    <p>Osman has held several leadership positions in esteemed international organizations. He served as the chairperson of the Advocacy & Communication Working Group Committee for the UNEP Faith for Earth Initiative Youth Council in Kenya. Additionally, he actively contributed as a committee member at the United Nations Youth Envoy, working closely with the UN Secretary-General's Envoy on Youth. His participation in the UNEP-Children and Youth Major Group underscored his commitment to global environmental initiatives.</p>\n                                    <h5><strong>Academic Achievements</strong></h5>\n                                    <p>Osman's academic pursuits are as impressive as his professional accomplishments. He graduated with a Bachelor of Education, majoring in Economics, from Milton Margai Technical University (MMTU) Education Centre. Currently, he is pursuing a Master's Degree with a major in Sustainable Humanitarian Actions at UCAM University in Murcia, Spain. His diverse skill set also includes a Professional Certificate in Project Management from the University of Las Vegas (UNLV).</p>\n                                    <h5><strong>Fellowships and Recognitions</strong></h5>\n                                    <p>Osman's dedication to sustainable development has earned him prestigious fellowships, including the Urban Leaders Fellowship (ULF) 2022 Cohort, Africa Climate School (ACS) 2021 Cohort, and the Anant Fellowship for Built Environment (AFBE) 2023 Cohort. His voluntary contributions to the Green Peace Corps and Earth Day 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization were honored with a Volunteer Service Award. Furthermore, he interned with the Global Shapers - Freetown Community Hub, demonstrating his commitment to local community engagement.</p>\n                                    <p>In summary, Osman Felix Cole stands as a beacon of environmental advocacy and sustainable development. His multifaceted career, international engagements, and academic pursuits underscore his unwavering commitment to creating a more sustainable and just world for future generations. His dedication and leadership in the environmental and climate justice arena continue to inspire positive change on a global scale.</p>\n                                    \n                                    \n                                    <div class=\"row progess-bar-item\">\n                                        <div class=\"col-md-3 col-6\">\n                                            <div class=\"single-skill\">\n                                       